#AI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="src/**"

LANGUAGE_RUNTIME:
- Rust stable (fill in version, e.g. "1.77")
- rust-toolchain.toml pins the toolchain — do not change without intent
- Nightly features require explicit opt-in and a comment justifying why

BUILD:
- cargo build
- cargo clippy -- -D warnings (clippy warnings are errors)
- cargo fmt --check

STYLE_CONVENTIONS:
- rustfmt is law — cargo fmt before committing
- clippy lints enforced — no `#[allow(...)]` without a comment
- Use thiserror for library errors, anyhow for application errors
- Prefer ? operator over explicit match on Results
- Document all public items with /// — at minimum a one-liner

FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS:
- No `unwrap()` or `expect()` in library code — propagate errors
- No unsafe blocks without a SAFETY comment explaining the invariant
- No `std::mem::transmute` without a very good reason and a comment
- No hardcoded secrets in source

EXPLICITLY_NOT_TOUCHING:
- (fill in: generated code, vendored crates, build.rs output, etc.)
